factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 4 problems
  Reel script says the bunk owner who sets the charging tariff was the initial proposal, which matches, but the reel_script states 'தடை ஏற்பட்டால் பங்க் உரிமையாளர்கள்தான் பொறுப்பேற்க நேரிடும்' (bunk owners will have to bear responsibility for outages) — the article says 'தலை உருளும்' and 'கெட்ட பெயர்' (their reputation would suffer), not a formal responsibility/liability claim
  Reel script omits the article's point that the owner-set-up model was replaced by oil companies using app-based charging, while mixing it with the tariff point; more importantly, the reel script and slides claim 'வணிக வளாகங்களில் சார்ஜிங் அமைப்பது வசதியாக இருக்கும்' as the dealers' demand, but the article says this is a suggestion that charging points could be set up at commercial complexes, cinemas and restaurants rather than bunks, which is a different framing
  Slide 4 states 'அப்படியானால் சார்ஜிங் அமைக்க டீலர்கள் தயார்' and the reel says dealers are ready 'if the government announces a clear policy', but the article conditions readiness on state-level infrastructure, investment and tariff policy together, and says low customer numbers are acceptable — the reel omits the 'குறைந்த கஸ்டமர்கள் வந்தாலும் பரவாயில்லை' qualifier
  Caption claims the bunk owners' association coordinator Rajasekhar said the government's policy would make them ready 'even if few customers come', which matches the article, but caption also attributes the commercial-complex suggestion to him without the article making clear it is his statement about bunks being unable to offer that facility
